means you will find all Local Bankruptcy Rules Forms in numerical and alphabetical sequence, starting with forms related to LBR 1002-1 to LBR 9075-1.  See link below\nL39:   * The remainder of LBR forms listed in the Central Guide are matched with the specific LBR that is related to that LBR form.\nL40:   * Note that a few forms apply only to a specific chapter in bankruptcy.  If so, the chapter number will be included in the form.  Otherwise, if there is no chapter number listed in the caption of a form, that form can be used in more than one chapter type.\nL41: \"Complete Set of TCG Supplements\" means you will find all 20 TCG Supplements in numerical order based on the number of the related FRBP Rule or LBR Rule.\nL42: \nL43: \"General Orders\" is a link to all orders that apply to all parties district wide; general orders can be entered in emergency situations or when it is clear the situation may change and the order process requires flexibility.  See link below\nL44: \"Public Notices\" is a link to notices that are posted several times each year to apprise the public of new or amended LBR, LBR Forms, and General Orders.  In addition, a Public Notice may identity dates when the court is closed.  See link below.\nL45: \nL46: \"Complete Set of FRBP\" means you will find a link to a database of all Federal Rules of Bankruptcy Procedure.\nL47: \"Complete Set of FRCP\" means you will find a link to a database of all Federal Rules of Civil Procedure.  Many of the FRCP apply in bankruptcy cases.  When this is true, a FRBP rule will indicate that a related FRCP rule applies.\nL48: \nL49: \nL50: \nL51: Section:\nL52: \nL53: Section 4 - Match Local Bankruptcy Rules with Forms\nL54: \nL55: Section Number or LBR Number:\nL56: \nL57: 1000\nL58: \nL59: Reference to Common Topics:\nL60: \nL61: cite6†Rules & Procedures L62: \nL63: Reference to Common Links:\nL64: \nL65: cite7†General Orders -- Complete Set L66: \nL67: cite8†Local Bankruptcy Rules -- Complete Set L68: 