ppellate Procedure. A committee of Ninth Circuit judges and lawyers propose changes to this court’s local rules.\nL40: \nL41: The following changes were adopted on December 1, 2025.\nL42: \nL43:   * cite14†December 2025 FRAP changes as adopted (PDF)†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L44: \nL45:   * cite15†December 2024 FRAP changes as adopted (PDF)†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L46:   * cite16†June 2026 Circuit Rule changes as adopted (PDF)†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L47: \nL48:   * cite17†December 2025 Circuit Rule changes as adopted (PDF)†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L49: \nL50:   * cite18†December 2024 Circuit Rule changes as adopted (PDF)†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L51: \nL52:   * cite19†December 2024 New 26.1-1 Disclosure Statement Circuit Rule changes as adopted (PDF)†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L53: \nL54:   * cite19†October 2024 Public comment (PDF)†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L55: \nL56: cite20†BROWSE ALL PAST RULE CHANGES L57: ## General Orders\nL58: \nL59: These are the internal operating procedures of the U.S. Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit.\nL60: \nL61: ### Download the U.S. Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit’s General Orders\nL62: \nL63: cite21†DOWNLOAD PDF†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L64: ## Administrative Orders\nL65: \nL66: These orders state how the court operates with respect to specific topics.\nL67: \nL68:   * cite22†June 16, 2023 Appellate Case Management System (PDF)†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L69: \nL70:   * cite23†September 20, 2022 Prisoner e-filing (PDF)†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L71: \nL72:   * cite24†May 24, 2021 Name Change (PDF)†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L73: \nL74:   * cite25†January 16, 2021 Highly Sensitive Documents (HSDs) (PDF)†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L75:   * cite26†February 1, 2019 Establishing the Criminal Justice Act (CJA) Unit (PDF)†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L76: \nL77:   * cite27†January 24, 2019 Suspending Deadlines for Paper Copies (PDF)†cdn.ca9.uscourts.gov L78: \nL79: cite28†BROWSE ALL PAST ADMINISTRATIVE ORDERS L80: ## Proposed Rules and Amendmen